From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:49:21 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 34/48] Plutonium: dock sites kept per project or everywhere

A site slot kept per project or everywhere has one browser tab, tagged with
its scope's tag (t3:project/<id>, t3:global). Its key or button brings that
tab into the thread it is pressed in, from the thread showing it (its preview
there closes without closing the tab), or opens one. The slot editor and the
tab menu set a site's scope as they do an app's; a tab put in the dock keeps
the scope it has.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
